at64\n  RNETMIG2023              float64\n  RNETMIG2024              float64\n  RNETMIG2025              float64\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914664232},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Now I understand the data:\n\n1. `farmers-markets` table has:\n   - `state_name`, `state_abbr`, and `farmers_markets` (number of farmers markets per state)\n\n2. `census-population` table has:\n   - `NAME` (state name), `SUMLEV` (summary level), and `POPESTIMATE2025` (2025 population estimate) among many others\n\nI need to:\n1. Get the total farmers markets (sum of all states)\n2. Get the total U.S. population\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n\nLooking at the census data, `SUMLEV` is likely a summary level code. I need to find which row represents the total U.S. population. Let me peek at the census data to understand it better.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Let me peek at the data to understand the structure better:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01AHpc38UEqv1z4i3kspgD5j","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"census-population","compose":"source.select('NAME', 'SUMLEV', 'POPESTIMATE2025').limit(10)"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01EGAGDxL39jw5gisvEdegr8","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers-markets","compose":"source.select('state_name', 'farmers_markets').limit(10)"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":427,"cacheRead":15732,"cacheWrite":1465,"totalTokens":17638,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.002135,"cacheRead":0.0015732,"cacheWrite":0.00183125,"total":0.00555345},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":192},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914664233,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77bryQEkC6vFiK2GhAi","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01AHpc38UEqv1z4i3kspgD5j","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"NAME\",\"SUMLEV\",\"POPESTIMATE2025\"\n\"United States\",10,341784857\n\"Northeast Region\",20,58042054\n\"New England\",30,15431980\n\"Middle Atlantic\",30,42610074\n\"Midwest Region\",20,69762666\n\"East North Central\",30,47693655\n\"West North Central\",30,22069011\n\"South Region\",20,133833983\n\"South Atlantic\",30,70198706\n\"East South Central\",30,20069188\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914670946},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01EGAGDxL39jw5gisvEdegr8","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_name\",\"farmers_markets\"\n\"California\",647\n\"New York\",555\n\"Pennsylvania\",426\n\"Minnesota\",390\n\"Illinois\",370\n\"Virginia\",336\n\"Wisconsin\",335\n\"Michigan\",321\n\"Massachusetts\",273\n\"Florida\",246\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914670946},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! I can see:\n1. The census data has \"United States\" as the first row with SUMLEV=10 and POPESTIMATE2025=341784857\n2. The farmers markets data is aggregated by state\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Sum all the farmers_markets values from the farmers-markets table\n2. Get the U.S. population (341,784,857 from the \"United States\" row with SUMLEV=10)\n3. Create a metric that calculates farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n\nLet me create a build script that joins these and calculates the metric. The farmers markets data should sum all state values, and the population is the U.S. total.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I'll create a build script to join these and calculate the metric. The key is that the farmers markets need to be summed by state, and we need the US total population:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01K2CpmNF363txWURX9UNoEF","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Read census data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census_population\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Get total farmers markets\nfm_total = fm.aggregate(total_farmers_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US total population (where NAME='United States' and SUMLEV=10)\nus_pop = (\n    census.filter(census.NAME == \"United States\")\n    .filter(census.SUMLEV == 10)\n    .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Join and calculate rate per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    fm_total.join(us_pop, fm_total.k == us_pop.k)\n    .mutate(farmers_markets_per_100k=fm_total.total_farmers_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"farmers_markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":805,"cacheRead":17197,"cacheWrite":680,"totalTokens":18696,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.004025,"cacheRead":0.0017197000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00085,"total":0.0066087},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":166},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914670946,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77cLStXtK8g9WFfFYHT","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01K2CpmNF363txWURX9UNoEF","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1354 bytes to .xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914678394},{"role":"assistant","content":